unit: dm-peer-outside-zero
commits: bd6355766 (the two renames)
what: the bar dm-peer-outside-fabric reads 0. Two stragglers remained outside
  commonwealth/crates/, each renamed per its DT [[noun]] row (identifiers only,
  no behaviour change):
    PeerHistory       -> TravelHistory       (sovereign-cli-llm/src/mesh_travel.rs:177, 8 refs / 1 file)
    PeerCanonicalLead -> CanonicalAtlasLead  (sovereign-daemon/src/auto_ingest.rs:1368, 4 refs / 1 file)
  Both are pub(crate) type definitions, which is what the census counts. The
  private PeerRow/PeerBody in mesh_travel.rs and the fn names carrying the word
  (peer_history, find_best_peer_canonical) are not type definitions, so they are
  not stragglers for this bar and are left as the DT [[noun]] rows do not name
  them. The DT [[noun]] rows keep the old `name` (the registry records what to
  rename, as PeerStore's row still does); no DT edit was needed.
checks: CLEAN exit=0 (disk gate, cache under threshold); LINT exit=0 (scoped to
  sovereign-cli-llm, sovereign-daemon, sovereign-cli, sovereign-cli-daemon,
  sovereign-cli-dev); CENSUS --self-test exit=0 (11 axes, 11/11 positives
  caught, 11/11 negatives refused).
census: peer-outside 2 in 2 crates -> 0 in 0 crates:
    peer-outside — Peer* definitions outside commonwealth/crates/ (the word anywhere in the name; prefix mode refused)
      value: 0 in 0 crates
    exit=0
